              <section class="workspace-handoff" aria-labelledby="workspace-handoff-title">
                <div class="framework-panel-heading"><div><span class="framework-panel-kicker">MANUAL HANDOFF · NO LIVE SYNC</span><h3 id="workspace-handoff-title">Save brief → Copy to Ramon → Run in DevLabs → Upload results here</h3></div><span class="workspace-sample-badge">PLANNED</span></div>
                <p>When owner storage is configured, the handoff will use the selected saved product, offer <strong>Run full core workflow</strong>, <strong>Resume from a stage</strong>, and <strong>Run one stage</strong>, and list only the approved input names, markets, and versions selected for that run. Site uploads and local DevLabs files are separate copies; download referenced inputs into the local product folder before dispatching. Ramon runs the workflow locally, and the owner uploads reviewed results back here.</p>
              </section>

              <div class="workspace-setup-requirements">
                <div class="framework-panel-heading"><div><span class="framework-panel-kicker">REQUIRED BEFORE PRIVATE DATA</span><h3>What needs to be configured</h3></div><span class="workspace-sample-badge">NOT SET UP</span></div>
                <ol>
                  <li><strong>Supabase project:</strong> create a project with Auth, Postgres, and Storage enabled. Configure owner-only email sign-in (for example, magic-link sign-in restricted to your email) and approved redirect URLs for localhost and the production domain.</li>
                  <li><strong>Database and row-level security:</strong> add product, source, stage-document/version, and resource metadata tables with an owner ID. Enable RLS and policies on every private table so only the signed-in owner can read or mutate their rows.</li>
                  <li><strong>Private object storage:</strong> create a non-public bucket such as <code>framework-private</code>. Scope paths to the owner and product, reject unauthorized uploads/downloads/replacements/exports, validate size and allowed types, and issue short-lived signed download links.</li>
                  <li><strong>Server-side Astro on Vercel:</strong> replace static-only output with the Astro Vercel server adapter and authenticated server endpoints/middleware. Check the owner session on every private record and file operation. Keep file bytes outside <code>public/</code> and the client bundle.</li>
                  <li><strong>Environment secrets:</strong> add <code>PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL</code> and <code>PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY</code> for client initialization under RLS, plus <code>SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY</code> only if server code requires elevated access. Store secrets in local <code>.env</code> (ignored by Git) and Vercel project environment settings; never prefix the service key with <code>PUBLIC_</code>/<code>VITE_</code> or expose it in browser code.</li>
                  <li><strong>Test before use:</strong> verify signed-out direct requests fail, owner requests can manage products/resources, two products and versions stay isolated, drafts do not replace approved files, uploads/downloads/exports work, and records persist across refresh, sign-out, and another device.</li>
                </ol>
                <p>Until those pieces are implemented and tested, the site offers only this static guide and clearly labeled sample data. No authentication or storage credentials have been added.</p>
              </div>
